think read the existing discovery handshake — an Introduction is minted and signed by an introducer, then accept() verifies it and upserts the introduced PeerId + descriptor into a bounded PeerTable; nothing chose a networking key yet
think built comlink/handshake_turn.rye to ask a crossing two questions in one breath — who are you (introduce.accept admits the peer) and which key do I seal to (turn_route.read_turn verifies the peer's turn under its identity key and takes the freshest); the peer's identity is the first 32 bytes of its peer id, its Kumara pubkey
think the two gates are deliberately independent — a peer admitted by a valid introduction still routes only to a verified, freshest key, so a replayed introduction cannot roll a live key backward and a forged turn cannot borrow an admitted identity
think it composes the existing introduce/table/descriptor with turn_route and the tilak without modifying them — a new integration module, cross-importing discovery/ and comlink/ siblings, which the build resolved
